{{--
  Breadcrumb trail: the visible nav and the BreadcrumbList JSON-LD, from one
  `crumbs` array so the two cannot drift.

  A crumb is { name, href?, url? } — the current page omits `href` and renders as
  plain text; `url` is the absolute form the JSON-LD needs.

  Usage: @include('breadcrumbs', { crumbs })

  Only the visible nav lives here. The matching BreadcrumbList JSON-LD is emitted
  by the marketing layout, because @push from inside an @include does not reach
  the parent's @stack — verified: the script tag simply disappears.
--}}
{{-- The shipped <Breadcrumb> renders the same trail inside a real <ol>/<li>,
     which the hand-written version above never had. aria-current on the last
     item and aria-hidden on the separators are preserved by the component.
     `crumbs` keeps its { name, href, url } shape because the layout's JSON-LD
     reads the same array; only the visible nav is mapped. --}}
<Breadcrumb className="shell subnav" :items="crumbs.map(c => ({ label: c.name, href: c.href }))" />
